1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,415
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,489
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,539 --> 00:00:18,465
Little Red Riding Hood and the Wolf!

7
00:00:23,045 --> 00:00:27,481
Once upon a time, in a stone
cottage at the edge of a village,

8
00:00:27,531 --> 00:00:32,820
there lived a cheerful, curious
girl who loved listening to stories.

9
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:36,660
Her grandmother, who lived
in the middle of the forest,

10
00:00:36,710 --> 00:00:42,082
had sewn her a red cape with a
hood, soft and warm like a hug.

11
00:00:42,742 --> 00:00:47,239
The girl loved the cape so much that
she never wanted to take it off,

12
00:00:47,311 --> 00:00:51,336
and so everyone in the village
called her Little Red Riding Hood.

13
00:00:51,964 --> 00:00:56,767
One spring morning, her mother packed
a wicker basket with an orange cake,

14
00:00:56,895 --> 00:01:00,920
a fresh loaf of bread and
a jar of golden honey.

15
00:01:01,505 --> 00:01:05,444
Your grandmother has a little cold, and
this cake will make her afternoon much

16
00:01:05,494 --> 00:01:06,407
happier,

17
00:01:06,457 --> 00:01:10,274
her mother said, covering
the basket with a blue cloth.

18
00:01:10,941 --> 00:01:15,015
I will take it right now, and I
will give Grandma the biggest hug,

19
00:01:15,065 --> 00:01:18,813
Little Red Riding Hood said,
bouncing with excitement.

20
00:01:19,394 --> 00:01:20,833
Then listen carefully:

21
00:01:20,883 --> 00:01:24,875
go straight along the path, do not
leave the trail, and do not talk to

22
00:01:24,925 --> 00:01:26,608
strangers in the forest,

23
00:01:26,658 --> 00:01:29,683
her mother said, looking into her eyes.

24
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:34,131
I promise, I will stay on the
path from beginning to end,

25
00:01:34,181 --> 00:01:38,095
Little Red Riding Hood said,
holding the handle of the basket.

26
00:01:38,716 --> 00:01:44,264
On the fence, a round brown owl with a
red bow on her head was listening very

27
00:01:44,314 --> 00:01:45,514
carefully.

28
00:01:46,063 --> 00:01:47,440
Hoo, hoo!

29
00:01:47,555 --> 00:01:52,049
A good promise is a promise kept, and
I will keep an eye on you from the

30
00:01:52,099 --> 00:01:53,199
treetops,

31
00:01:53,249 --> 00:01:56,301
Popcorn said, spreading her wings.

32
00:01:57,375 --> 00:02:01,839
Little Red Riding Hood walked into
the forest, and the sun made golden

33
00:02:01,889 --> 00:02:04,581
patterns on the ground between the leaves.

34
00:02:07,474 --> 00:02:11,660
Birds were singing, squirrels were
hopping from branch to branch,

35
00:02:11,710 --> 00:02:15,416
and the girl skipped along
the trail, humming a song.

36
00:02:16,068 --> 00:02:21,713
Suddenly, from behind an enormous tree,
out stepped a grey wolf with a bushy

37
00:02:21,763 --> 00:02:24,177
tail and pointy ears.

38
00:02:24,723 --> 00:02:28,540
Good morning, young lady in the red
hood, what a lovely morning for a walk in

39
00:02:28,590 --> 00:02:30,395
the forest, don't you think?

40
00:02:30,445 --> 00:02:33,706
the wolf said, with a very fancy bow.

41
00:02:34,334 --> 00:02:38,470
Little Red Riding Hood did not know
that the wolf was a sneaky trickster,

42
00:02:38,542 --> 00:02:43,053
so she answered politely,
because he seemed so friendly.

43
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:46,934
Good morning, Mister Wolf, I am
taking this basket to my grandmother,

44
00:02:46,984 --> 00:02:48,774
because she has a cold,

45
00:02:48,824 --> 00:02:51,891
Little Red Riding Hood said with a smile.

46
00:02:52,409 --> 00:02:56,709
And where does your grandmother live,
my dear, so far away from everything?

47
00:02:56,759 --> 00:03:00,812
the wolf asked, his eyes
shining with curiosity.

48
00:03:01,473 --> 00:03:06,166
She lives in the middle of the forest,
in a house under three big oak trees,

49
00:03:06,216 --> 00:03:08,058
with a hazel hedge in front,

50
00:03:08,108 --> 00:03:11,577
Little Red Riding Hood
said, pointing far away.

51
00:03:12,235 --> 00:03:17,366
Up on her branch, Popcorn opened her
big eyes wide and shook her head,

52
00:03:17,416 --> 00:03:20,774
because the girl had just
told her plans to a stranger.

53
00:03:21,858 --> 00:03:26,669
The wolf looked around and had a very
sneaky idea, which made his bushy tail

54
00:03:26,719 --> 00:03:28,689
swish from side to side.

55
00:03:29,242 --> 00:03:33,046
Just look at all these pretty flowers,
my dear, your grandmother would be so

56
00:03:33,096 --> 00:03:34,882
happy with a colorful bunch,

57
00:03:34,932 --> 00:03:37,374
the wolf said in a sweet voice.

58
00:03:38,017 --> 00:03:41,597
Little Red Riding Hood looked
at the meadow and saw yellow,

59
00:03:41,697 --> 00:03:47,111
purple, pink and blue flowers swaying
in the wind as if they were dancing.

60
00:03:47,740 --> 00:03:52,003
That's true, Grandma loves flowers, and
a bunch of them will go perfectly with

61
00:03:52,053 --> 00:03:53,222
the orange cake,

62
00:03:53,272 --> 00:03:56,769
Little Red Riding Hood said,
stepping off the trail.

63
00:03:57,393 --> 00:04:01,821
While the girl picked flowers,
farther and farther from the path,

64
00:04:01,893 --> 00:04:06,890
the wolf raced away along a shortcut,
straight to Grandma's house.

65
00:04:06,997 --> 00:04:08,373
Hoo, hoo!

66
00:04:08,454 --> 00:04:12,988
Little Red Riding Hood, your mother
asked you not to leave the path,

67
00:04:13,038 --> 00:04:13,890
remember?

68
00:04:13,940 --> 00:04:17,465
Popcorn said, swooping down close to her.

69
00:04:18,086 --> 00:04:23,258
The girl jumped, looked at the trail
far away, and remembered the promise she

70
00:04:23,308 --> 00:04:24,736
had made to her mother.

71
00:04:25,372 --> 00:04:29,685
You're right, Popcorn, the flowers
distracted me, and now I'm going back to

72
00:04:29,735 --> 00:04:31,563
the path as fast as I can,

73
00:04:31,613 --> 00:04:35,013
Little Red Riding Hood
said, picking up her basket.

74
00:04:36,095 --> 00:04:40,628
Meanwhile, the wolf reached the
house under the three oak trees,

75
00:04:40,678 --> 00:04:44,939
straightened his ears and
knocked on the door, very gently.

76
00:04:46,669 --> 00:04:50,467
Who is knocking on my door,
right in the middle of my nap?

77
00:04:50,517 --> 00:04:55,250
the grandmother asked from inside,
her voice croaky from her cold.

78
00:04:55,792 --> 00:05:00,039
It's me, Grandma, your granddaughter,
Little Red Riding Hood,

79
00:05:00,089 --> 00:05:02,043
and I've brought you an orange cake,

80
00:05:02,093 --> 00:05:05,154
the wolf said, trying to
make his voice very high.

81
00:05:05,823 --> 00:05:09,704
But the grandmother was very clever,
and she peeked through the side window

82
00:05:09,754 --> 00:05:14,140
and saw a grey, bushy tail
swishing behind the door.

83
00:05:14,730 --> 00:05:19,644
My granddaughter does not have a tail,
and certainly not such a bushy one,

84
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:24,241
the grandmother whispered to herself,
and she hurried into the big wardrobe in

85
00:05:24,291 --> 00:05:25,491
her bedroom.

86
00:05:26,510 --> 00:05:31,030
The wolf pushed the door, which
was not locked, and went inside,

87
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,466
but he did not find anyone.

88
00:05:34,116 --> 00:05:38,747
So he opened Grandma's drawer, put on
a frilly white nightcap and a pair of

89
00:05:38,797 --> 00:05:43,975
round glasses, and climbed into bed,
pulling the quilt up to his nose.

90
00:05:44,596 --> 00:05:48,546
A little later, Little Red
Riding Hood came up the path,

91
00:05:48,596 --> 00:05:52,677
with the basket in one hand and
the bunch of flowers in the other.

92
00:05:55,575 --> 00:06:00,053
She thought it was strange that the
door was open, so she went in slowly,

93
00:06:00,103 --> 00:06:03,086
calling for her grandmother
in a calm voice.

94
00:06:03,719 --> 00:06:06,537
Grandma, it's me, your
granddaughter, I've brought cake,

95
00:06:06,587 --> 00:06:09,524
bread, honey and a bunch of wildflowers,

96
00:06:09,574 --> 00:06:13,015
Little Red Riding Hood said,
walking into the bedroom.

97
00:06:13,671 --> 00:06:18,496
In the bed, Grandma looked very different,
so the girl came closer and looked

98
00:06:18,546 --> 00:06:19,746
carefully.

99
00:06:20,191 --> 00:06:24,149
Oh, Grandma, what big ears you have
today, under that white nightcap,

100
00:06:24,199 --> 00:06:27,224
Little Red Riding Hood
said, tilting her head.

101
00:06:27,805 --> 00:06:30,560
All the better to hear
your voice, my dear,

102
00:06:30,610 --> 00:06:34,357
the wolf answered in a
strange, squeaky voice.

103
00:06:35,041 --> 00:06:38,356
And what big eyes you have,
behind those round glasses,

104
00:06:38,406 --> 00:06:41,917
Little Red Riding Hood
said, taking a step back.

105
00:06:42,478 --> 00:06:45,011
All the better to see you with, my dear,

106
00:06:45,061 --> 00:06:49,253
the wolf answered, holding
the quilt with his furry paws.

107
00:06:49,868 --> 00:06:53,894
And what big, hairy hands you
have, with such long nails,

108
00:06:53,944 --> 00:06:56,608
Little Red Riding Hood said, frowning.

109
00:06:57,178 --> 00:06:59,666
All the better to hug you with, my dear,

110
00:06:59,716 --> 00:07:03,339
the wolf answered, smiling
with all his teeth.

111
00:07:03,951 --> 00:07:08,521
And what an enormous mouth you have,
Grandma, I have never seen so many teeth

112
00:07:08,571 --> 00:07:09,430
at once,

113
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:12,894
Little Red Riding Hood said,
holding the basket tight.

114
00:07:13,876 --> 00:07:18,185
All the better to eat your orange
cake faster, and the whole basket too!

115
00:07:18,235 --> 00:07:21,121
the wolf said, jumping out of bed.

116
00:07:21,761 --> 00:07:26,183
But the wolf got all tangled up in the
long quilt, tripped over the frilly

117
00:07:26,233 --> 00:07:29,980
nightcap and fell on the floor
with his legs in the air.

118
00:07:31,707 --> 00:07:36,023
At that very moment, the
wardrobe door creaked open,

119
00:07:36,109 --> 00:07:40,121
and out stepped the grandmother,
with a wooden spoon in her hand.

120
00:07:40,716 --> 00:07:45,538
You sneaky wolf, in this house nobody
eats my granddaughter's cake without

121
00:07:45,588 --> 00:07:46,905
asking first!

122
00:07:46,955 --> 00:07:50,813
the grandmother said, banging
the wooden spoon on a pot.

123
00:07:51,450 --> 00:07:54,642
Little Red Riding Hood ran
to her grandmother's side,

124
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:58,656
and the two of them held
hands, strong and brave.

125
00:07:59,254 --> 00:08:00,630
Hoo, hoo!

126
00:08:00,733 --> 00:08:02,110
Hoo, hoo!

127
00:08:02,214 --> 00:08:06,605
Help, help, there's a clumsy
wolf in Grandma's house!

128
00:08:06,655 --> 00:08:11,736
Popcorn said, flying in through
the window and hooting very loudly.

129
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:20,133
Nearby, a woodcutter was chopping wood,
and when he heard the owl hooting,

130
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:23,828
he came running down the
trail, blowing his horn.

131
00:08:26,745 --> 00:08:30,658
Who is making all this fuss at Grandma's
house, right in the middle of the

132
00:08:30,708 --> 00:08:31,646
forest?

133
00:08:31,696 --> 00:08:35,360
the woodcutter asked in
a deep, strong voice.

134
00:08:35,992 --> 00:08:39,956
The wolf wriggled out of the quilt,
still wearing the white nightcap,

135
00:08:40,006 --> 00:08:44,392
and ran out the door, so embarrassed
that he didn't even look back.

136
00:08:44,945 --> 00:08:48,606
I'm never coming back here, never
ever, because in this house even the

137
00:08:48,656 --> 00:08:51,350
grandmas and the owls are far too clever!

138
00:08:51,400 --> 00:08:55,008
the wolf said, vanishing among the trees.

139
00:08:55,624 --> 00:09:00,963
Grandma, Little Red Riding Hood and
Popcorn laughed so hard that even the

140
00:09:01,013 --> 00:09:05,510
woodcutter let out a big laugh,
holding on to his green hat.

141
00:09:06,126 --> 00:09:10,565
Now tell me, young lady, how did a
wolf find the way to your grandmother's

142
00:09:10,615 --> 00:09:11,448
house?

143
00:09:11,498 --> 00:09:14,357
the woodcutter asked with a kind smile.

144
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:18,667
I told him, because he seemed friendly,
and then I even left the path to pick

145
00:09:18,717 --> 00:09:19,602
flowers,

146
00:09:19,652 --> 00:09:23,608
Little Red Riding Hood said,
looking down at her boots.

147
00:09:24,225 --> 00:09:29,289
Everybody makes mistakes sometimes, my
dear, and what matters is to learn from

148
00:09:29,339 --> 00:09:31,762
them and be more careful next time,

149
00:09:31,812 --> 00:09:35,670
the grandmother said, stroking
her granddaughter's braids.

150
00:09:36,746 --> 00:09:41,252
Late in the afternoon, Little Red
Riding Hood's mother arrived too,

151
00:09:41,302 --> 00:09:45,155
because she missed her daughter and
wanted to make sure everything was all

152
00:09:45,205 --> 00:09:46,405
right.

153
00:09:46,600 --> 00:09:51,050
Grandma set up a wooden table in the
garden, and they all sat down together to

154
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:55,597
share the orange cake, the fresh
bread and the tea with honey.

155
00:09:56,249 --> 00:10:00,108
Mom, I learned that it's very
important to stay on the path,

156
00:10:00,158 --> 00:10:02,678
and that we never tell
our plans to strangers,

157
00:10:02,728 --> 00:10:05,892
Little Red Riding Hood
said, hugging her mother.

158
00:10:06,506 --> 00:10:10,746
And I learned that an orange cake tastes
even better when you share it with

159
00:10:10,796 --> 00:10:12,206
the people you love,

160
00:10:12,256 --> 00:10:15,976
the grandmother said, who no longer
seemed to have a cold at all.

161
00:10:16,617 --> 00:10:20,956
From that day on, Little Red Riding
Hood visited her grandmother every

162
00:10:21,006 --> 00:10:26,108
Saturday, always along the right path,
and the wolf never showed up in those

163
00:10:26,158 --> 00:10:27,378
parts again.

164
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:33,386
And Popcorn, up on the branch of the
oak tree, nibbled her piece of cake,

165
00:10:33,472 --> 00:10:36,205
blinking her big eyes with happiness.

166
00:10:43,527 --> 00:10:44,727
The End.

167
00:10:46,441 --> 00:10:47,153
Hoo...

168
00:10:47,203 --> 00:10:48,228
Psst!

169
00:10:48,278 --> 00:10:49,850
Are you still awake?

170
00:10:50,004 --> 00:10:52,057
Did you like tonight's story?

171
00:10:52,147 --> 00:10:56,577
Little Red Riding Hood showed us that
it is important to listen to the people

172
00:10:56,627 --> 00:11:01,564
who care for us, to stay on the right
path, and to never tell our plans to

173
00:11:01,614 --> 00:11:02,925
strangers.

174
00:11:03,215 --> 00:11:07,521
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

175
00:11:07,817 --> 00:11:12,715
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

176
00:11:12,765 --> 00:11:15,170
for more stories at bedtime.

177
00:11:15,474 --> 00:11:16,674
Hoo...

